                <pb facs="0587" n="563" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v24/pg563"/>

                <head>259. Memorandum From the President’s Military Representative (Taylor) to the President’s Special
                    Assistant for National Security Affairs (Bundy)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d259-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-01-05">January 5,
                        1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In the course of the meeting today of the 5412 Special Group, we discussed the
                    items of business which should be taken up at the 9:30 meeting tomorrow on
                        Laos.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d259-f2"/> They appear to be the following: <pb
                        facs="0588" n="564" xml:id="pg564"/>
                    <list>
                        <label>a.</label>
                        <item>A presentation by State of the alternatives facing us in Laos: <list>
                                <label>(1)</label>
                                <item>“Persuade” Phoumi to
                                    play ball by the technique suggested in the 5412 paper which you
                                    have seen.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d259-f3"/></item>
                                <label>(2)</label>
                                <item>Get rid of Phoumi.</item>
                                <label>(3)</label>
                                <item>Desist in our efforts to form a Souvanna Phouma government.</item>
                            </list></item>
                        <label>b.</label>
                        <item>An estimate by CIA of the probable
                            enemy reaction to a break-off in negotiations.</item>
                        <label>c.</label>
                        <item>A JCS estimate of the increased
                            military capabilities of the Royal Laotian Army supported by indigenous
                            tribesmen.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>You may want to work up a formal agenda based upon the foregoing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">M.D.T.</hi><anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d259-f4"/></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Attached hereto is a round-up made by Lt. Commander Bagley of activities going on today at
                        State and Defense.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d259-f5"/></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
